WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.150
Start with one use case and one audience.

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:14.853
Personal productivity, research support, document review, coding, security analysis, private knowledge search, and workflow automation have different data, quality, latency, and control requirements.

00:00:14.853 --> 00:00:18.129
Describe the job in observable terms.

00:00:18.129 --> 00:00:31.016
Instead of build a general assistant, define tasks such as summarize approved meeting notes, answer questions from internal guides with citations, or draft code changes for human review.

00:00:31.016 --> 00:00:32.545
Set boundaries.

00:00:32.545 --> 00:00:43.685
Identify data the assistant may access, actions it may take, systems it may call, users it may serve, and decisions it must not make.

00:00:43.685 --> 00:00:47.835
High-impact actions need stronger review, authorization, and audit.

00:00:47.835 --> 00:00:51.111
Define success before choosing a model.

00:00:51.111 --> 00:01:01.377
Measures may include answer correctness, citation support, edit quality, completion rate, latency, user time saved, privacy compliance, and the cost of mistakes.

00:01:01.377 --> 00:01:04.217
Map expected inputs and outputs.

00:01:04.217 --> 00:01:11.862
PDFs, markdown, code, images, speech, structured records, and tool results each change infrastructure and interface needs.

00:01:11.862 --> 00:01:16.449
Sensitive data classifications may prohibit some components or deployments.

00:01:16.449 --> 00:01:20.599
Expand only after the first workflow is reliable.

00:01:20.599 --> 00:01:26.060
Adding more documents, users, tools, agents, and automation multiplies failure paths.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:31.957
A narrow useful assistant earns the evidence needed for a broader one.

00:01:31.957 --> 00:01:35.670
Assign a product owner and data owner.

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:46.373
Someone must decide priorities, accept quality, approve sources, handle user reports, authorize access, and stop a workflow when risk or maintenance exceeds value.
